        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: NCAA, Notre Dame, California, Georgia, Harvard, Princeton\n- People: George Gipp, Walter Camp\n- Events: 1920 NCAA football season\n- Concepts: national champions, All-American honors\n\nFacts:\n- The 1920 NCAA football season had no clear-cut champion.\n- The Official NCAA Division I Football Records Book lists California, Georgia, Harvard, Notre Dame, and Princeton as national champions for the 1920 NCAA football season.\n- Notre Dame was led during the 1920 NCAA football season by George Gipp.\n- George Gipp was Notre Dame's first Walter Camp All-American.\n- George Gipp was nicknamed \"The Gipper.\"\n- George Gipp died before the end of 1920.",
